In one simple sentence
In your SOC lab, you learned:

attack my own machine → collect logs → detect

In this cloud lab, you will learn:

build cloud system → attack it safely → see AWS logs/alerts → fix the design so it is harder to attack

That is why we are building it. EC2 gives you the server, IAM controls who can do what, CloudTrail records activity, GuardDuty looks for suspicious behavior, and Security Groups act like the firewall. 
